WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.820
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.290
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.290
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.210
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.420
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:12.870
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.180
Takara Fansubs

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.970
<i>Angeletta is a child of the most famous family in Milan, the Montovernis.</i>

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:38.110
<i>But... Countess Isabella, also known as the "Ice Queen",</i>

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:42.890
<i>...persisted in her belief that Angeletta sought the Montoverni estate.</i>

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:48.470
<i>Romeo exploded angrily when he heard her harshness.</i>

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.180
Episode 22:

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.180
I Meet Grandmother!

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.990
Now show me proof of Angeletta's so-called "pure heart".

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.850
Your life is on the line.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:11.630
People tend to shed "pure hearts" when a large fortune is involved.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.610
Angeletta is no different.
She wants the Montoverni estate.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:24.860
Angeletta is different!

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.840
Very well. Then show me proof.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.710
Countess!

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:37.230
Will you believe in Angeletta if I allow myself to be shot?

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.120
Romeo!

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.840
Madam Isabella, the boy doesn't know what he's saying.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:49.440
He asked for it. He must take responsibility for his own words.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.150
But this is going too far!

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.020
I accept responsibility!

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:02.640
So be it.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.500
Stop, Madam Isabella!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.630
Madam Isabella.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.980
What foolishness.
You could have escaped.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:28.740
Teach this boy some manners so we won't have this insolence again.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.390
Yes, madam.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.920
Madam! Is everything all right?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:48.490
You damn fool! Give some thought to what might have happened to you!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.430
I'm sorry.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.670
Anyway, thank goodness you weren't hurt.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:54.750
Still...

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.850
I was sincere about proving it to her. So why didn't she shoot me?

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.310
You'd rather have been shot?

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:08.850
At the time, yes... But I admit I was pretty scared.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.890
You're hopeless.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:21.590
Madam Isabella didn't plan to shoot you. She only wanted to test you.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.360
Test me?

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.170
You may have passed, actually.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.350
Passed? How do you know?

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:35.300
We're old friends, and I can guess just by looking at her face.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:42.640
Do you also know about Angeletta's mother and father?

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.240
Wanna know about it?
- Yes.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:55.490
Angeletta's father, Lord Adolf, was a splendid man.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:04.570
Kind and intelligent since childhood, he was his mother's pride and joy.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:10.280
All of his mother's love was devoted to him during his childhood,

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:15.000
...and he developed into a perceptive and gentle young man.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:19.230
But something unexpected happened...

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.660
Mother.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:29.240
This is my girlfriend, Giovanna.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.380
How do you do, Madam.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:41.980
Adolf had fallen in love with a poor but beautiful girl named Giovanna,

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.100
...and soon they bore a child together.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:51.480
Adolf welcomed them both into the Montoverni house,

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.360
...but Isabella never gave her approval.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:58.200
The honor of the Count's name was everything to her.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.940
Soon Adolf left.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:12.680
It wasn't long after that the news arrived.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.330
The young parents fell victim to a disease and passed on,

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:22.470
...leaving behind Angeletta, still an infant.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.480
Let's go home, Romeo. It's late.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.940
I don't get it.

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.810
She throws away her own granddaughter,

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:40.170
...and never tries to meet her!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.670
It just doesn't make sense to me!

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.740
Nobility comes with its own set of obligations.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.620
It's not our place to speak.
- But...

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.190
Give it up!

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.690
It's the way of the world.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.700
But boss!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.080
But... but boss...

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:09.840
...it's not fair to Angeletta!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:29.560
What beautiful eyes that boy had.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:33.690
But we'll probably never meet again.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.160
<i>Angeletta, I never knew...</i>

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.840
<i>You're all alone.</i>

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.160
<i>I'll always be with you.</i>

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.180
"Heaven"?!

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.470
What's this about Heaven?

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:14.260
No! This is Angeletta's dairy.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:24.980
Sorry. I didn't mean to look, I just...

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.890
"Heaven", was it?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:35.670
"These days my body seems to be getting weaker every day."

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.490
Angeletta!
- Listen, Romeo!

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:46.670
"Very soon I may join Father and Mother in Heaven."

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.230
Don't say that!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.750
I'm prepared for it.
Because of my illness.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:12.790
"When I consider that, I forget all my sorrows,

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.860
...and I'm filled with happiness."

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:18.760
"And I have only one final dream to be fulfilled."

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.210
Your final dream?

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:23.210
Don't. Show me your usual smile.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:26.910
Will you hand me the music box?

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:32.010
Thank you.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.850
This belongs to Grandmother.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:36.590
Madam Isabella?

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.310
Father sent it to her as a birthday present.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:50.920
I listen to this song as if it were a lullaby sung by Grandmother...

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:56.670
And I imagine the color of her eyes... her hair...

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:00.000
...how she looks when she laughs.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.670
It would be nice if she looks like me.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.430
I look at this sunset and think,

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.040
"Grandmother must be looking at the same sky right now."

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.200
Just thinking that way...

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.500
I'm flooded with dreams.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.600
And the courage to live wells up inside me.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.380
Angeletta!

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:35.640
Angeletta, hold on. I'll call the boss.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:36.570
Romeo.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.340
To be honest... I want to meet her.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.190
I know. It's a selfish dream.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.890
But I'd like to meet her... just once.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.540
Before my illness gets any worse.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.900
Then let's go to the mansion and meet her.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:01.600
I'll take you. To the mansion.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:02.820
I promise.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:04.650
Romeo!

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.250
Angeletta! Don't talk anymore!

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.710
Boss! Come quick! It's Angeletta!

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:30.260
Thank goodness it was only a minor attack.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:36.610
But the doctor scolded us for allowing you to get so excited.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:38.810
You've got to be more careful.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:41.020
I'm sorry, Mother.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:44.920
It's because you talk too much with that Romeo.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:48.440
That's enough. Just let the child rest.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.610
Rest up, Angeletta.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.180
Yes.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:03.760
What? Bring Angeletta to the Montoverni estate?

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:08.210
"Ice Queen" or no, she just needs to meet Angeletta,

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.000
...and I'm sure she'll like her.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:15.180
But what if dragging her out there winds up hurting her?

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:18.290
I know. But it must be done.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:19.520
Romeo...

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:27.020
Alfredo, it's possible... this will be Angeletta's last dream.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.180
Last dream?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:34.030
<i>To be honest... I want to meet her.</i>

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:37.440
<i>I know. It's a selfish dream.</i>

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.430
<i>But I'd like to meet her... just once.</i>

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:46.900
<i>Before my illness gets any worse.</i>

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.230
If we don't take her now,

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:53.310
...she may never have the chance to meet Lady Isabella.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.680
All right. I'll come with you.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.070
Alfredo!

00:12:58.580 --> 00:12:59.660
I'm going too!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.390
So am I.
- Me too.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:08.060
What's that surprised look for?
We're saying we'll go.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:10.110
It's for Angeletta's sake.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:12.660
Right. She's one of us!

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.710
Thanks, you guys!

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:17.270
All right! Then tonight's the night!

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.280
Yeah!

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:27.410
I must say, Angeletta is really and truly an ANGEL.

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:32.220
Thanks to her I get this treasure each and every time.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:33.560
I'm trying to sleep.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.080
What a pleasant feel it has!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.420
My treasure, my treasure.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.180
Come in.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.180
Time to go, Angeletta.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.660
Don't stare like that.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.740
It's because I'm meeting Grandmother for the first time.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.550
Do I look silly?

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.070
No.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:11.230
Sorry, it's just that you're so pretty. Isn't she, Piccolo?

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:27.780
Don't worry, Angeletta.
I'm right beside you.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:28.620
Me too.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:31.620
Thank you Dante, Michaelo.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.130
I'm ready for a fight.

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:36.950
Is it far?
- It's just ahead.

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:44.400
<i>Angeletta has only honesty in her heart.</i>

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:48.960
<i>Will you believe in Angeletta if I allow myself to be shot?</i>

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:51.900
What's the matter with me?

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:56.260
I can't get that boy's words out of my head.

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:07.390
Adolf, are you urging me on...

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.730
...to meet Angeletta, your orphan child?

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:17.800
We want to see Lady Isabella. Please let us in.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:22.780
Don't make me laugh! This is no place for you kids. Go home!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:27.580
If you just tell her we've brought Angeletta, she should understand.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.190
Angeletta?

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.970
We've brought the Princess.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:37.720
No chance! I haven't heard anything about this.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.840
Get out of here before I call the cops.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.590
Wait, please! Let us see...

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.680
Thank you.

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.360
It's all right. Let's go home.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.040
Angeletta!

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.870
I'm more than satisfied to have come this far.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.690
It's made me very happy.
Everybody, thank you.

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:12.700
It's a waste of time trying to reason with an adult like that.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:16.160
Romeo, take me home.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:19.200
No, it's still too early to give up.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.200
We're the Black Brothers.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:26.720
If we work together, you'll get to meet your grandmother, Angeletta.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:32.320
Adolf, I've felt so lonely since I lost you.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.020
You should know what it's like for me.

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:42.040
I've lost a loved one...

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:49.140
Adolf... yet you still say to meet this child?

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:08.860
Now comes the tough part.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.820
Come on in, Your Highness.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:17.420
Hey! What are you doing there?

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.270
Hey! Stop!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:28.460
Romeo, you take Angeletta and get inside. We'll distract the enemy.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:29.690
Got it.

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:31.940
Where'd that kid go?

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.750
Hey, hey! Over here!

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.970
No, over here.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.000
When did you...?!
- There's one over here, too!

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.070
Here too!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.880
Who are you kids?!

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:47.790
We're the Black Brothers!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.550
Yahoo!

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:56.010
Just a bit farther, Angeletta. You can do it.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:59.250
What the devil's going on here?

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:00.930
Well...

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:04.390
Why you little...!
- What's the meaning of this?!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.930
Yahoo!

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:07.100
I'm sorry...

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:11.240
...sorry that we had to resort to this.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.200
But we have a good reason.

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.170
So long.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.750
Later.
 -One moment!

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:21.640
What's wrong, Pops?

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:24.690
Why you!!
- Sorry!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.390
You'll see Madam Isabella very soon.

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:30.950
Let me rest a minute, Romeo.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:35.730
Are you all right, Angeletta?

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:41.750
I'm so happy... Father was born in this house.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.850
Is an attack coming on?
Angeletta! That's it, isn't it!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:48.730
I'm okay. Just let me rest a moment.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.110
It would be OK...

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:54.640
...to die right here.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.380
Angeletta!

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:58.740
I'm with you...

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.900
...and I have my wish.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.690
I love you, Romeo.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.800
Me too, Angeletta.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.760
We can go now, Romeo.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.200
Angeletta! Hold on!

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:35.570
Romeo... take me to Grandmother...

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.440
What's next, Alfredo?

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.070
We wait for Romeo.

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:47.960
I hope Angeletta gets to meet her.
- Yeah.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.840
Wait here. I'll go look for Madam Isabella.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:53.670
Romeo.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:56.640
Thank you.

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:58.390
I'm fine now.

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:07.620
Piccolo, where are you going?

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.410
Come back, Piccolo!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:19.660
Piccolo, there you are. Come along.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.540
What's wrong, Piccolo?

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:26.090
My!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.840
Now now, Piccolo. Be nice.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:35.240
Don't be scared. Come here.

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:41.150
Good boy, now come here.

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:43.180
Easy, boy.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:45.180
Come.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:50.580
I'm Angeletta. What's your name?

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.160
That tickles!

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:04.820
Adolf.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:08.590
Madam Isabella?

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:16.810
I'm Angeletta.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.800
I... ah...

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:22.250
Why have you come here?

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.330
I wanted to meet you...

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.800
Go home this instant.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:32.900
I admit you're the living likeness of Adolf.

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:36.820
But you should never have come here.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.960
Go home... right now!

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.180
<i>Angeletta got to meet her grandmother...</i>

00:21:56.200 --> 00:22:00.780
<i>...but she passed out and fell into a deep sleep.</i>

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:04.840
<i>Fight it, Angeletta!
Open your eyes!</i>

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:11.050
See you then!

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:11.050
<i>Farewell, My Angel</i>

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:11.050
Next time:

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:16.740
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:25.350 --> 00:22:29.450
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:33.750
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:37.950
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:47.060
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:50.960
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:58.260
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:03.860
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:08.060
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
